.TH YUMED 8 "2026-05-09" "YUME 1.0" "YUME Manual"
.SH NAME
yumed \- YUME server daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yumed
[
.B --config
.I path
]
[
.I options
]
.PP
.B yumed
.B completion
.B bash
.PP
.B yumed
.B --help
.br
.B yumed
.B --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B yumed
is the YUME server. It listens for authenticated YUME clients, validates
their auth keys, negotiates transport capabilities, and opens outbound
target sockets for allowed streams. It can also serve a real HTTP facade
for non-YUME requests, enforce anonym/no-log mode, manage authorized
keys, and expose relay/directory features when enabled.
.SH BASIC SETUP
.PP
.nf
sudo yumed \
    --listen 443 \
    --cert /etc/yume/server.crt \
    --key /etc/yume/server.key \
    --auth-keys /etc/yume/authorized_keys
.fi
.PP
Port 443 requires root or
.BR cap_net_bind_service .
After binding, the daemon can drop privileges unless
.B --root
is used.
.SH CORE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--config " path
Read server configuration from a JSON file.
.TP
.BI "--listen " port
Listen port.
.TP
.BI "--cert " path
TLS certificate.
.TP
.BI "--key " path
TLS private key.
.TP
.BI "--auth-keys " path
Authorized client public keys.
.TP
.BI "--threads " n
Worker thread count. Use
.B 0
for automatic selection.
.TP
.BI "--reverse-port-min " port
Minimum port for reverse forwards.
.TP
.BI "--reverse-port-max " port
Maximum port for reverse forwards.
.TP
.BI "--dns-server " ip
Resolver for outbound opens.
.TP
.B --robots-deny
Serve
.B /robots.txt
as
.B Disallow: /
through the existing HTTP facade. Disabled by default.
.TP
.BI "--filter-list " spec
Load a source or egress filter list. The form is
.BI client|egress|both:allow|deny:path
where
.I path
is JSON,
.B vpn_db.bin ,
or a
.B .tar.xz
archive containing one of those files.
.TP
.BI "--filter-geolite " path
Country lookup archive, GeoLite2-Country
.B .mmdb ,
or compact YUME
.B geoip_country_ipv4.db .
Archives are extracted at startup; hot-path lookup is in-memory.
.TP
.BI "--filter-memory-mib " n
Approximate memory cap for loaded filter data. Use
.B 0
for unlimited.
.TP
.BI "--client-filter-mode " mode
Client source filter mode:
.B blacklist
or
.BR whitelist .
.TP
.BI "--egress-filter-mode " mode
Destination filter mode:
.B blacklist
or
.BR whitelist .
.TP
.BI "--packet-egress " tun
Enable packet-native egress over an operator-prepared Linux TUN/NAT
interface. Disabled by default.
.TP
.BI "--packet-tun-name " ifname
TUN device to attach for packet-native mode. Default:
.BR yume-pkt0 .
.TP
.BI "--packet-cidr " cidr
IPv4 pool assigned to packet-native clients. Default:
.BR 10.89.0.0/24 .
The .1 address is reserved for the TUN side.
.TP
.BI "--packet-mtu " n
Packet-native MTU. Default:
.BR 1420 .
.TP
.B --obfs
Enable HTTP/2 carrier obfuscation.
.TP
.BI "--obfs-secret " string
Secret used to validate obfs path tokens.
.TP
.B --allow-local-ip
Allow private and loopback destinations when key policy permits it.
.TP
.B --control-full
Allow unrestricted server-side network control when compile-time and
key-policy gates also permit it.
.TP
.B --root
Keep root privileges.
.TP
.B --boring
Use minimal logs.
.TP
.B --timing
Emit lightweight timing diagnostics.
.SH SECURITY OPTIONS
.TP
.B --inner
Enable inner PQ crypto. Kept for compatibility; prefer
.B --inner-heavy
or
.BR --inner-light .
.TP
.B --no-inner
Disable inner crypto and hopping.
.TP
.B --inner-heavy
Use the heavy KDF path when available.
.TP
.B --inner-light
Use the light KDF path.
.TP
.B --inner-dual
Accept heavy and light clients.
.TP
.B --inner-required
Reject clients that do not negotiate inner crypto.
.TP
.B --hop
Enable live inner key hopping.
.TP
.B --no-hop
Disable live inner key hopping.
.TP
.BI "--hop-interval " ms
Set key hopping interval in milliseconds.
.TP
.BI "--pq-key " path
PQ private key for inner crypto.
.TP
.B --pq-auto-generate
Generate a PQ keypair when needed.
.TP
.B --use-embedded-master
Allow the embedded BaseFWX master fallback. This is for explicit
test/development use, not production.
.TP
.B --no-embedded-master
Disable the embedded BaseFWX master fallback.
.SH HTTP FACADE AND ANONYM OPTIONS
.TP
.B --real
Serve real HTTP for non-YUME requests on the same port.
.BI "--real-index " path
HTML file served for
.BR / .
.TP
.BI "--real-secret " string
Hidden metadata secret used by YUME tooling.
.TP
.BI "--real-secret-file " path
Load or create a real-facade secret file.
.TP
.B --anonym
Enable anonym mode. This removes identifying log fields where supported.
.TP
.BI "--anonym-proof-mode " mode
Proof policy:
.BR auto ,
.BR local ,
or
.BR fixcraft .
.TP
.BI "--anonym-api " url
Verity API URL.
.TP
.BI "--anonym-token " string
Verity API token.
.TP
.BI "--anonym-ca-key " path
Anonym CA private key.
.TP
.BI "--anonym-ca-cert " path
Anonym CA certificate.
.TP
.BI "--anonym-sub-key " path
Anonym sub-CA private key.
.TP
.BI "--anonym-sub-cert " path
Anonym sub-CA certificate.
.SH RELAY AND DIRECTORY OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--server-name " name
Display name for this server.
.TP
.BI "--server-id " 32hex
Stable server endpoint ID.
.TP
.B --relay-enable
Enable client relay features.
.TP
.B --relay-disable
Disable client relay features.
.TP
.B --directory-enable
Enable endpoint directory.
.TP
.B --directory-disable
Disable endpoint directory.
.TP
.BI "--operator-keys " path
Operator key metadata file.
.TP
.B --federation-enable
Enable static federation mode.
.TP
.BI "--peer " json
Add a federation peer.
.TP
.B --attach-local
Attach to a local running
.B yumed
instance.
.SH APPLICATION CODEC OPTIONS
Application codecs are protocol-aware shims, not raw TCP forwards. The
server must allow a codec globally and the client key must list it in
.BR auth_keys.meta .
.TP
.BI "--codec-allow " name
Allow an application codec id or alias (for example
.BR monero-rpc ).
Repeat for multiple codecs.
.TP
.B --allow-monero-rpc
Legacy alias for
.BI "--codec-allow " monero-rpc .
.TP
.BI "--monero-rpc-backend " host:port
Loopback backend for Monero RPC reconstruction. Default:
.BR 127.0.0.1:18089 .
Only loopback literals are accepted.
.SH DISGUISE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--hide-in-the-crowd " profile
Serve canned HTTP responses for non-YUME HTTPS probes using a named
disguise profile. Profiles mimic common CDN or static-site error pages
instead of closing immediately after TLS.
.SH FEDERATION AND CLUSTER OPTIONS
Federation links are mutual TLS 1.3 connections between
.BR yumed (8)
peers. Each peer keeps its own
.B authorized_keys
and
.BR auth_keys.meta .
.TP
.B --cluster-bootstrap
Mark this node as a cluster bootstrap that accepts incoming peer dials.
Implies
.BR --federation-enable .
.TP
.BI "--cluster-join " spec
Dial a peer using the short form
.BI [id@]host[:port][?pin=sha256] .
Bracket IPv6 addresses as
.BR [2001:db8::1]:443 .
Repeat for multiple peers.
.TP
.B --public-node
Advertise this node in the directory when directory features are enabled.
.TP
.BI "--federation-auth-key " path
Ed25519 private key used to authenticate federation peer links.
.TP
.BI "--federation-anonym-ca " path
CA certificate peers must present for federated TLS.
.TP
.BI "--peer " json
Add a federation peer using raw JSON (power-user form).
.SH SESSION LIMITS
.TP
.BI "--tls-handshake-timeout-ms " ms
Abort slow TLS handshakes after
.I ms
milliseconds.
.TP
.BI "--max-sessions" n
Cap concurrent authenticated client sessions.
.TP
.BI "--accept-rate-limit " n
Limit new TCP accepts per second (0 disables).
.SH AUTH_KEYS.META FORMAT
.B auth_keys.meta
is JSON keyed by Ed25519 public-key fingerprint (hex). Each entry may
include an
.B alias
and a
.B permissions
object. Omitted permission fields default to deny for dangerous
features and allow for relay-side chat/file/bytes channels.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.nf
{
  "0d4f3a...fingerprint...": {
    "alias": "alice",
    "permissions": {
      "allow_exec": true,
      "allow_local_ip": true,
      "allow_codecs": ["monero-rpc"],
      "control_full": false,
      "allow_inbound_admin": true,
      "allow_outbound_admin": false,
      "allow_chat": true,
      "allow_file": true,
      "allow_bytes": true
    }
  }
}
.fi
.PP
Generate fingerprints with
.BI "yumed --auth-keys " path " --keys-list" .
See
.BR docs/PERMISSIONS.md
for the full field table.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B YUME_DNS_SERVER
Override the resolver used for server-side outbound opens when
.B --dns-server
is not set.
.TP
.B YUME_ANONYM_LOCAL_SIGN
When set to
.BR 0 ,
disable local anonym proof signing even if CA/sub keys are configured.
Set to
.B 1
to force local signing on platforms where it is off by default.
.TP
.B SUDO_UID
.BR /
.B SUDO_GID
When started under
.BR sudo ,
these are read after bind/listen so PQ key files can be
.BR chown (2)
ed before privilege drop.
.SH KEY MANAGEMENT
.TP
.B --keys-list
List authorized keys.
.TP
.BI "--keys-add " pub.pem
Add an authorized public key.
.TP
.BI "--keys-remove " id
Remove an authorized key by fingerprint or alias.
.TP
.BI "--keys-alias " id " " alias
Set or update a key alias.
.TP
.BI "--keys-gen " prefix
Generate an Ed25519 keypair as
.IR prefix .key
and
.IR prefix .pub .
.TP
.B --keys-gen-add
Append the generated public key to
.BR auth_keys .
.TP
.B --ui
Open the interactive server manager.
.SH AUTHORIZATION MODEL
Dangerous server features are behind three gates:
.IP 1. 4
compile-time feature switches, such as
.BR YUME_FEATURE_EXEC ;
.IP 2. 4
runtime server flags, such as
.BR --allow-local-ip ;
.IP 3. 4
per-key metadata in
.BR auth_keys.meta .
.PP
A key without metadata can authenticate, but dangerous permissions default
to deny.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start a basic server:
.nf
sudo yumed --listen 443 --cert /etc/yume/server.crt \
    --key /etc/yume/server.key --auth-keys /etc/yume/authorized_keys
.fi
.TP
Require inner crypto:
.nf
sudo yumed --listen 443 --cert server.crt --key server.key \
    --auth-keys authorized_keys --inner-heavy --inner-required \
    --pq-key /etc/yume/master_pq.sk
.fi
.TP
Enable obfs and real HTTP facade on the same port:
.nf
sudo yumed --listen 443 --cert server.crt --key server.key \
    --auth-keys authorized_keys --obfs --obfs-secret shared \
    --real --real-index /var/www/yume/index.html
.fi
.TP
Block VPN-provider egress destinations using an operator-supplied archive:
.nf
sudo yumed --listen 443 --cert server.crt --key server.key \
    --auth-keys authorized_keys \
    --filter-list egress:deny:/etc/yume/vpn_db.tar.xz \
    --filter-geolite /etc/yume/GeoLiteCountry.tar.xz
.fi
.TP
Generate and add a client key:
.nf
yumed --auth-keys /etc/yume/authorized_keys --keys-gen /tmp/alice --keys-gen-add
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/yume/authorized_keys
Authorized client public keys.
.TP
.I /etc/yume/auth_keys.meta
Per-key permissions and metadata.
.TP
.I /etc/yume/vpn_db.tar.xz
Optional private VPN-provider blocklist archive. This file is
operator-supplied and should not be committed to the YUME source tree.
.TP
.I /etc/yume/
Common system configuration directory.
.TP
.I config/yumed.json
Example local server configuration.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/yume/
Installed documentation in packaged builds.
.SH INSTALLATION
From a build tree:
.PP
.nf
cmake -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
cmake --build build -j$(nproc)
sudo cmake --install build
.fi
.PP
Manual man-page install:
.PP
.nf
sudo install -Dm644 docs/man/yumed.8 /usr/local/share/man/man8/yumed.8
sudo mandb
.fi
.PP
Debian package builds produced by CPack install this page automatically.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR yume (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR tor (1),
.BR systemd.service (5)
